  "articleBody": "Installing a toilet grab bar seems simple, but there are a few common slip-ups that can make it unsafe or ineffective. First off, a huge no-no is installing it into just drywall or tile. Those materials won't hold up to the weight you'll put on a grab bar! You absolutely need to anchor it into studs or some serious blocking behind the wall. Another big mistake is thinking a towel bar or a suction-cup product will do the trick. They’re just not designed for the kind of load-bearing support a proper grab bar provides. Placing the bar too high or too low is another common issue; it should be around 33-36 inches from the floor for most people. If it’s not at a comfortable height, it won't be much help. Lastly, leaving the toilet area cluttered with stuff that obstructs the grip zone defeats the whole purpose. Keep the area clear so you can easily reach and use the bar. If you're feeling unsure about any of these steps, especially locating studs or drilling into tricky surfaces like tile, it’s always smart to bring in a pro. HH Remodeling LLC has experience with these kinds of installations and can ensure everything's safe and sound.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
